rs:\n1. \"Integer Echo State Networks: Efficient Reservoir Computing for Digital Hardware\" - Focuses on using ESNs in digital hardware for efficient computation.\n2. \"Evolutionary Echo State Network: evolving reservoirs in the Fourier space\" - Discusses evolving ESNs in the Fourier domain for anomaly detection.\n\nBoth papers explore the application of ESNs in anomaly detection but from different perspectives. ESNs are trained by random initialization and not during the learning process, which makes them efficient for real-time data processing.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":773,"prompt_eval_duration":45414000,"total_duration":2651615000}}